From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: keep the PCM backend format

sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup() adds S16_LE to the backend format mask.
params_format() takes the lowest set bit, so every PCM backend ran at
16 bit and a 24 bit stream was truncated in the DSP. Set S16_LE only
when the mask is empty, which is the compressed playback case the
fixup was added for. PCM backends keep the frontend format.

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
index f193d0b..e9dbbee 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -66,7 +66,8 @@ static int sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	channels->min = channels->max = 2;
-	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+	if (snd_mask_empty(fmt))
+		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
 
 	return 0;
 }
